The key observation is:

\[
a_i = b_i - b_{i+1} + b_{i+2} - b_{i+3} + \cdots
\]

Adding \(a_i\) and \(a_{i+1}\) cancels everything except \(b_i\):

\[
a_i + a_{i+1} = b_i
\]

For the last element:

\[
a_n = b_n
\]

So:

\[
b_i = a_i + a_{i+1} \quad (1 \le i < n)
\]
\[
b_n = a_n
\]

This gives an \(O(n)\) solution.

